# App UI non-negotiables

These are the always-on rules. For the full how-to (spacing scale, typography, icons, MCP workflow), the **`app-ui` skill** carries the detail — activate it whenever you build or restyle UI.

## shadcn-first

- Always reach for a shadcn component from `@/components/ui/*` before hand-rolling markup. Compose with variants and sub-components (`CardHeader`, `DialogTitle`, etc.).
- Add missing primitives with `pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add <name>` — don't copy-paste component source from docs.
- Build bespoke markup only when no shadcn primitive fits. Say so in your reasoning when you do.
- For generic shadcn composition rules (forms, overlays, gap vs space-y), follow the **`shadcn` skill** — do not duplicate them here.

## Design tokens, never raw color

- Never hardcode hex/rgb/oklch in components. Use semantic tokens: `bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border-border`, `bg-muted`, `text-destructive`, etc.
- The token registry is `resources/css/app.css` (`:root`, `.dark`, `@theme inline`). Brand intent lives in `.ai/design/brand.md`.
- Add new colors in `app.css` before using them in TSX.

## Reuse before creating

- Check `resources/js/pages`, `resources/js/components`, and sibling feature files for an existing pattern before writing a new one.
- Use full Card/Dialog/Form composition — see **`DemoA.tsx`** / **`DemoB.tsx`** and the **`app-ui` skill** `rules/spacing-layout.md`.

## Verify APIs

- Confirm shadcn component APIs with `user-shadcn` MCP or `pnpm dlx shadcn@latest docs <component>` before writing them — do not guess props or sub-component names.
